From: jalsarraf0 <19882582+jalsarraf0@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell: reserve panel space on the screen the panel follows

availableScreenRect() and availableScreenRegion() only subtract a panel
when the panel's QWindow::screen() is the screen being asked about. On
Wayland that is the oldest output the panel's surface entered. When a
second output overlaps the panel's monitor (a KVM, capture dongle or TV
at the same position) and KWin lists it first, the panel window lands
on that output and its space is never reserved on its own screen, so
the desktop icon grid runs under the panel.

Compare against PanelView::screenToFollow(), as the rest of ShellCorona
already does.

Sent to KDE as "shell: reserve panel space on the screen the panel
follows" (plasma/plasma-workspace, master); same change, plus an
autotest. Unchanged in Plasma/6.7, Plasma/6.8 and master as of
2026-10-10.
---
 shell/shellcorona.cpp | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/shell/shellcorona.cpp b/shell/shellcorona.cpp
index c33387b..8687206 100644
--- a/shell/shellcorona.cpp
+++ b/shell/shellcorona.cpp
@@ -1219,7 +1219,7 @@ QRegion ShellCorona::_availableScreenRegion(int id) const
     }
 
     return std::accumulate(m_panelViews.cbegin(), m_panelViews.cend(), QRegion(screen->geometry()), [screen](const QRegion &a, const PanelView *v) {
-        if (v->isVisible() && screen == v->screen() && v->visibilityMode() != PanelView::AutoHide) {
+        if (v->isVisible() && screen == v->screenToFollow() && v->visibilityMode() != PanelView::AutoHide) {
             // if the panel is being moved around, we still want to calculate it from the edge
             return a - v->geometryByDistance(0);
         }
@@ -1287,7 +1287,9 @@ QRect ShellCorona::_availableScreenRect(int id) const
     int topThickness, leftThickness, rightThickness, bottomThickness;
     topThickness = leftThickness = rightThickness = bottomThickness = 0;
     for (PanelView *v : m_panelViews) {
-        if (v->isVisible() && v->screen() == screen && v->visibilityMode() != PanelView::AutoHide) {
+        // Not QWindow::screen(): with overlapping outputs it is whichever one the compositor
+        // reported first, which may not be the screen the panel is on
+        if (v->isVisible() && v->screenToFollow() == screen && v->visibilityMode() != PanelView::AutoHide) {
             switch (v->location()) {
             case Plasma::Types::LeftEdge:
                 leftThickness = accumulator(leftThickness, v->totalThickness());
